# Papuma.Kernel Sample — diagnostics and the MCP endpoint via httpYAC.
#
# The MCP section uses the Streamable-HTTP protocol, stateless (the default since
# the MCP C# SDK 2.0): every request stands alone — no Mcp-Session-Id header, and
# the server rejects one with 400. `initialize` is optional; it shows the
# negotiated protocol and capabilities. Responses arrive as text/event-stream —
# httpYAC displays them fine.

### Health (includes the change-feed lag check)
GET {{host}}/health

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### MCP (observability.md: the diagnostics surface for AI agents)

### MCP 1: initialize (optional in stateless mode — protocol and capabilities)
POST {{host}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2025-06-18",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": { "name": "httpyac", "version": "1.0" }
  }
}

### MCP 2: list the Papuma tools
POST {{host}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "method": "tools/list"
}

### MCP 3: feed lag per handler (both feeds)
POST {{host}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 3,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "get_feed_lag",
    "arguments": {}
  }
}

### MCP 4: the Art.-30 model inventory (types, policies, keys, retentions)
POST {{host}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 4,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "get_model_inventory",
    "arguments": {}
  }
}

### MCP 5: a document history, scope-bound and policy-applied
# Paste an order id from shop.http here:
@orderId = paste-an-order-id-here
POST {{host}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 5,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "get_document_history",
    "arguments": {
      "documentType": "Order",
      "documentId": "{{orderId}}",
      "tenantId": "demo"
    }
  }
}

### MCP 6: failure table of both feeds (poison candidates)
POST {{host}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 6,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "get_feed_failures",
    "arguments": {}
  }
}
